WEBVTT

00:06.881 --> 00:09.092
[opening theme song playing]

00:45.086 --> 00:47.380
[waves crashing]

00:55.847 --> 00:57.974
[light music playing]

00:58.057 --> 01:00.018
[Ha-kyung] Signals are simple.

01:00.101 --> 01:01.686
[beeping]

01:01.770 --> 01:04.147
Sometimes, they're sounds.

01:05.023 --> 01:07.192
Sometimes, they're colors.

01:09.819 --> 01:12.030
- [thunder rumbles]
- [rain pouring]

01:21.414 --> 01:22.874
[thunder roaring]

01:31.883 --> 01:33.885
[phone vibrates]

01:33.968 --> 01:34.803
HA-KYUNG

01:34.886 --> 01:37.889
And sometimes, they're vibrations.

01:37.972 --> 01:44.020
They keep signaling to me
that nothing is safe in this world.

01:44.103 --> 01:45.688
[line ringing]

01:45.772 --> 01:52.779
EPISODE 1
SIGNAL

01:56.449 --> 01:58.076
- [Tae-kyung] No answer?
- Mm.

01:58.159 --> 01:59.869
[phone vibrates]

02:00.620 --> 02:03.081
[Ki-jun] Sorry. I don't think
I can make it to the hanbok store.

02:03.164 --> 02:05.291
- I'm not feeling good.
- [Tae-kyung] What is it?

02:06.334 --> 02:08.169
Ki-jun doesn't feel so great today.

02:08.753 --> 02:09.754
Or he's upset.

02:11.131 --> 02:12.215
"Upset"?

02:13.383 --> 02:15.009
[sighs]
About yesterday.

02:15.635 --> 02:17.262
Why did she drag him around for that long?

02:17.345 --> 02:19.848
Not only drag him around.
[sighs]

02:19.931 --> 02:23.393
All day long, she kept
messing around with his ego.

02:23.476 --> 02:26.312
Mm, if I was him, I'd be
so appalled, I'd call the wedding off.

02:26.396 --> 02:28.690
Oh, I'd be grateful for that.

02:28.773 --> 02:30.692
- Mom.
- [grunts]

02:30.775 --> 02:33.486
It's hard these days
to find a decent man, you know.

02:33.570 --> 02:36.531
A steady paycheck,
pension guaranteed at retirement,

02:36.614 --> 02:39.242
guaranteed you'll never starve.

02:40.118 --> 02:42.912
[Tae-kyung] That's why
she's marrying him. It's his stability.

02:42.996 --> 02:45.498
At least be a little reliable
for her, you know.

02:45.582 --> 02:48.501
I barely dragged him around all yesterday,
and now he's not feeling great?

02:48.585 --> 02:50.753
I feel fantastic and I'm almost 70.

02:51.337 --> 02:52.922
[Mrs. Bae] "Stability" my ass!

02:53.006 --> 02:55.508
[Tae-kyung] Just think of it
as fate for them.

02:55.592 --> 02:58.720
Mom, look, they've been together
ten whole years without one fight.

02:58.803 --> 03:00.847
Yeah. And that's also not good.

03:00.930 --> 03:04.142
I'm her mother,
and even I can't stand her attitude.

03:04.225 --> 03:05.810
Even if he's so in love,

03:05.894 --> 03:08.104
it's a little suspicious
he never gets irritated.

03:08.187 --> 03:10.773
It's true love. It's true!

03:10.857 --> 03:13.401
Couples argue to show
they love each other.

03:14.652 --> 03:16.070
This one, I like it.

03:16.154 --> 03:18.531
- Yeah, it's pretty.
- The color is really beautiful.

03:18.615 --> 03:20.867
Excuse me.

03:21.576 --> 03:23.202
- [shop owner] Ah, yes, ma'am.
- Ah!

03:23.286 --> 03:24.704
- Right this way.
- Thanks.

03:26.581 --> 03:28.249
[sighs]

03:28.333 --> 03:31.711
[forecaster] Daytime temperatures today
are up over three degrees nationwide.

03:31.794 --> 03:33.338
Expect more of sunny skies.

03:33.421 --> 03:35.506
We've got scattered clouds
across the region right now.

03:35.590 --> 03:36.758
But they're almost cleared up,

03:36.841 --> 03:40.428
and then it stayed clear and bright
for a good while after that.

03:40.511 --> 03:43.473
Air quality is high,
so enjoy that spring sunshine.

03:43.556 --> 03:45.767
- Lovely weather in Seoul with a height…
- Are we there yet?

03:45.850 --> 03:46.935
- …of 18 degrees.
- Huh?

03:47.018 --> 03:49.020
But it's a light midday breeze,
too, for a little afternoon…

03:49.103 --> 03:51.064
- Oh, up there, turn left.
- We will have the weather

03:51.147 --> 03:52.899
you wish you could have every day.

03:52.982 --> 03:57.153
[forecaster] As the sunshine continues,
brush conditions will get drier.

03:57.237 --> 03:58.655
So, everyone, watch those embers…

04:06.704 --> 04:08.206
You said we were going for tea.

04:08.957 --> 04:10.124
We are here for tea.

04:11.668 --> 04:14.545
- Is this a teahouse, Mom?
- What makes something a teahouse?

04:14.629 --> 04:16.965
If we're inside and drinking tea,
that makes it a teahouse.

04:17.048 --> 04:18.383
[water sloshes]

04:21.719 --> 04:23.054
[exhales]

04:23.137 --> 04:26.182
What are you seeking?
What has brought you here today?

04:26.266 --> 04:28.893
Uh, my daughter, I mentioned her earlier.

04:28.977 --> 04:31.688
- Oh, this is her.
- You know, she's a deaconess.

04:32.272 --> 04:33.523
"Deaconess?"

04:33.606 --> 04:37.235
Deaconess, pastor, doctor,
reverend, professor.

04:37.318 --> 04:40.530
All titles people seek
when they have a conflicted heart.

04:42.073 --> 04:44.701
- [paper rustles]
- Oh, here.

04:47.036 --> 04:50.415
Mm. Both born under the Red Hare.

04:51.374 --> 04:52.917
[chiming]

04:53.001 --> 04:54.794
Year and hour of the hare.

04:55.461 --> 04:56.754
[whistles]

05:02.510 --> 05:06.514
Being too cautious
can cause some problems in your life.

05:07.640 --> 05:10.727
She's so skeptical
ever since she was little.

05:10.810 --> 05:13.938
She'd even smell the cup
before she'd have a drink of water.

05:14.022 --> 05:16.649
I just don't want to turn out
like Papa. What's wrong with that?

05:16.733 --> 05:17.817
Hey now.

05:17.900 --> 05:19.736
Mom's just worried about you.

05:19.819 --> 05:22.864
And you should know your true
astral compatibility before you marry.

05:22.947 --> 05:24.991
So you got divorced
'cause the stars weren't aligned?

05:25.074 --> 05:27.577
[gasps]
Ha-kyung, don't say that.

05:27.660 --> 05:28.661
So your daughter.

05:29.871 --> 05:31.456
You're obviously a little cautious.

05:31.539 --> 05:33.875
A little cautious.
Yes, you're right. She is.

05:33.958 --> 05:37.253
More than a little.
It's almost an affliction.

05:37.337 --> 05:42.341
But an astral connection can't be avoided
just because you're cautious.

05:42.425 --> 05:44.552
[bells jingle]

05:47.430 --> 05:49.766
- [thumps]
- [exhales]

05:50.558 --> 05:51.392
What? What now?

05:51.476 --> 05:54.270
- The husband's journey…
- [Mrs. Bae] What about it?

05:55.772 --> 05:57.982
His relationship with his spouse
isn't great.

05:58.066 --> 05:59.942
[psychic] Also, I can see
yang-in energy in him.

06:00.026 --> 06:02.779
His wife, he could lose her.

06:03.362 --> 06:04.906
- A dead wife?
- Divorce?

06:04.989 --> 06:06.032
[hums]

06:06.115 --> 06:07.784
[gong clanks]

06:07.867 --> 06:09.577
Ah, I was right.

06:09.660 --> 06:12.121
I told you something was wrong
about him from the beginning.

06:12.205 --> 06:13.790
- I'm done here.
- Hey, Ha-kyung.

06:13.873 --> 06:15.208
- Stay and hear her out.
- Let go!

06:15.291 --> 06:16.334
- Hey!
- I paid a lot of money for this.

06:16.417 --> 06:18.961
[psychic] Bring that umbrella over there.

06:19.670 --> 06:21.631
- Why?
- [clattering]

06:23.049 --> 06:24.425
It's going to rain.

06:25.093 --> 06:26.219
[scoffs]

06:26.302 --> 06:29.806
[mysterious music playing]

06:38.397 --> 06:40.441
[birds chirping]

06:46.364 --> 06:47.657
Rain? I don't think so.

06:52.453 --> 06:55.123
[light music playing]

06:55.998 --> 06:57.458
SI-WOO

06:57.542 --> 06:59.627
[Si-woo] Si means time and woo means rain.

06:59.710 --> 07:01.671
It means rain that comes on time.

07:01.754 --> 07:05.258
Hmm. So that's why woo is used for rain.

07:05.341 --> 07:08.594
Ah, you know, as a name,
it's not really done.

07:08.678 --> 07:12.223
Oh! My grandfather
was a farmer his whole life.

07:12.306 --> 07:15.768
He said that nothing's more precious
than rain that comes just in time.

07:16.811 --> 07:19.397
And, uh, why do you need a seal?

07:19.480 --> 07:20.648
[exhales]

07:23.359 --> 07:24.444
I'm buying a new car.

07:24.527 --> 07:26.529
[upbeat music]

07:27.155 --> 07:28.823
STAMP SEALS

07:45.381 --> 07:47.008
[beeps]

08:00.229 --> 08:01.731
[chimes]

08:01.814 --> 08:03.065
[automated woman voice] Doors opening.

08:04.192 --> 08:06.319
[heels clacking]

08:06.402 --> 08:08.404
[automated woman voice] Doors closing.

08:11.866 --> 08:13.576
[beeping]

08:17.538 --> 08:18.789
PASSCODE ERROR

08:20.875 --> 08:23.669
[doorbell clicks, chimes]

08:29.967 --> 08:31.469
- [objects clinking]
- [door lock beeps]

08:32.178 --> 08:34.597
Oh! What are you doing here right now?

08:34.680 --> 08:36.766
You said you weren't feeling good. Here.

08:36.849 --> 08:39.185
I'm feeling better after a cold shower.

08:39.268 --> 08:40.353
Uh-huh. That's good to hear.

08:41.729 --> 08:43.523
How come you changed the door code?

08:44.982 --> 08:46.859
Oh, uh, that's…

08:47.527 --> 08:49.153
My mom barged in on you, huh?

08:51.197 --> 08:53.366
- [chuckles]
- Sorry.

08:53.449 --> 08:56.327
- Ah, you comin' in?
- I gotta get to work.

08:56.410 --> 08:58.037
[Ha-kyung] I'm already running late.

08:58.120 --> 08:59.247
- Just a sec.
- [phone vibrates]

09:01.749 --> 09:02.792
I've got to run.

09:02.875 --> 09:04.502
- Make sure you eat the porridge.
- Mm.

09:06.254 --> 09:07.588
[automated woman voice] Doors opening.

09:08.673 --> 09:10.550
Hello. Jin Ha-kyung speaking.

09:11.384 --> 09:12.635
[automated woman voice] Doors closing.

09:14.804 --> 09:16.264
[doors close]

09:19.475 --> 09:21.561
[Seok-ho]
You should report to the Director.

09:21.644 --> 09:23.646
I thought we said
we wouldn't talk about that.

09:23.729 --> 09:25.731
Come on, though. For real. It's hail.

09:26.274 --> 09:28.859
The serious hail,
there'd be guaranteed city damage.

09:28.943 --> 09:31.988
So we need to run analysis
and even if it's just one percent chance.

09:32.071 --> 09:34.991
So, Asst. Director, what's the probability
from your initial tracking?

09:35.992 --> 09:37.952
- You wanna hear a number?
- [Ha-kyung] Yes.

09:39.203 --> 09:41.122
Around nearly five percent.

09:41.205 --> 09:43.165
Okay. And without a round nearly?

09:45.209 --> 09:46.877
[sighs]

09:46.961 --> 09:48.045
HAIL RADAR

09:49.880 --> 09:52.133
Somewhere between 4.8 and 4.9.

09:52.216 --> 09:54.385
So you're telling me
it's still under five percent.

09:54.468 --> 09:56.387
I'm saying it's super close, though.

09:56.470 --> 09:58.055
Well, circle back
when it's really five, okay?

09:58.139 --> 10:00.349
We really should do this by the book.
You understand?

10:00.433 --> 10:01.934
[groans]

10:04.312 --> 10:05.688
[phone clacks]

10:05.771 --> 10:07.440
She acts like she's the director.

10:07.523 --> 10:09.233
[beeping]

10:15.656 --> 10:17.533
DIRECTOR CHOI JONG-SU

10:33.549 --> 10:36.177
[vehicle honks]

10:49.273 --> 10:52.360
[playful music playing]

10:52.443 --> 10:54.612
On your way to work, Reporter Chae?

10:59.283 --> 11:01.369
- What's with the car?
- I bought it.

11:02.161 --> 11:04.497
- With what money?
- I got a three-year loan.

11:05.331 --> 11:06.457
[sighs]

11:06.540 --> 11:08.459
Come on. Get in, huh?

11:08.542 --> 11:09.960
[chuckles]
I gotta go.

11:10.753 --> 11:11.962
[seat belt clicks]

11:14.382 --> 11:16.550
They already wrapped up
the morning forecast

11:16.634 --> 11:17.843
and it's almost lunchtime.

11:18.636 --> 11:20.471
You gotta eat something, right, hmm?

11:22.431 --> 11:23.724
So let's go.

11:24.809 --> 11:27.103
[sirens wailing]

11:40.074 --> 11:41.450
It's not new?

11:42.493 --> 11:44.203
It's essentially new.

11:44.286 --> 11:45.788
[Si-woo] Just a little not new.

11:47.832 --> 11:49.750
[honking]

12:04.598 --> 12:06.559
[light music playing]

12:06.642 --> 12:09.103
You saw this place on TV and you said
you wanted to come here.

12:09.728 --> 12:10.855
[Si-woo] What do you think?

12:10.938 --> 12:12.731
Your boyfriend's so observant, huh?

12:12.815 --> 12:14.442
[awkward chuckle]
Oh.

12:17.111 --> 12:18.279
Oh, you're back.

12:18.362 --> 12:19.822
[nervously]
Uh…

12:22.908 --> 12:26.203
- We'll have the number two Couple Special.
- Great. Couple number two.

12:26.287 --> 12:27.913
Mm-hmm.

12:28.581 --> 12:29.790
[footsteps receding]

12:29.874 --> 12:33.085
- You've been here before?
- Uh, with a friend.

12:34.295 --> 12:35.921
Ah. Oh, well.

12:36.005 --> 12:38.215
I wanted to bring you for your first time.

12:38.299 --> 12:39.383
Mm.

12:39.467 --> 12:40.801
That was so long ago.

12:40.885 --> 12:43.429
Now that I've got a car,
I'll start taking you out more.

12:44.096 --> 12:45.389
What would you like to go do?

12:46.515 --> 12:48.184
Mm, I don't know.

12:48.267 --> 12:50.269
[sucks teeth]
Mm…

12:51.103 --> 12:52.313
Ah! Road trip?

12:53.606 --> 12:57.026
It's summer soon.
Let's go before it gets too crazy.

12:58.944 --> 13:00.488
A few days ago,

13:00.571 --> 13:03.324
there was a faint signal
on the adiabatic report.

13:03.407 --> 13:04.325
You know that one?

13:05.576 --> 13:07.119
In the middle of March, a snow warning?

13:07.203 --> 13:09.038
Right away, I knew that it had to be hail.

13:09.121 --> 13:11.248
I knew I had to find the data
to back up my report,

13:11.332 --> 13:13.501
so I spent most
of three whole days in the…

13:16.253 --> 13:17.630
[keypad clacking]

13:19.215 --> 13:20.216
Ah.

13:21.967 --> 13:23.260
You like Gapyeong, right?

13:23.344 --> 13:24.929
[Si-woo] There are so many
cute cafés there.

13:25.012 --> 13:28.265
We could bring a tent and cookware
and camp outside somewhere with a view.

13:28.349 --> 13:31.393
I know everything there is about
the geography and weather over there.

13:31.477 --> 13:33.521
Uh, camping's not for me.

13:35.314 --> 13:37.274
Or a vacation rental?
Bet there's a good one.

13:37.942 --> 13:39.652
- [keypad clacks]
- [sighs]

13:42.530 --> 13:43.614
Okay, uh…

13:43.697 --> 13:46.116
[loud clonking]

13:48.786 --> 13:49.828
[hail patters]

13:49.912 --> 13:51.080
[Si-woo] Damn.

13:51.163 --> 13:53.415
Hail. No way.

13:54.250 --> 13:55.251
Oh.

13:55.334 --> 13:57.086
The forecast was clear.

13:57.169 --> 13:59.171
- [thunder rumbles]
- [sighs]

13:59.255 --> 14:00.422
They ignored us again.

14:04.510 --> 14:07.304
[frantic music playing]

14:10.516 --> 14:13.561
[clacking]

14:16.313 --> 14:17.898
[honking]

14:17.982 --> 14:19.900
[tires screeching]

14:24.530 --> 14:25.948
[ripping]

14:27.950 --> 14:31.662
[ominous music playing]

14:39.086 --> 14:43.132
PREVENT FOREST FIRES

14:46.844 --> 14:48.095
Situation Room, do you copy?

14:48.178 --> 14:51.849
The hail is damaging the helo airframe.
Repeat. Helicopter airframe damaged.

14:53.225 --> 14:54.643
[cracks]

15:04.987 --> 15:06.196
[phones ringing]

15:06.280 --> 15:09.450
INNOVATIVE WEATHER SERVICES
A STEPPING STONE TO PUBLIC SAFETY

15:09.533 --> 15:11.994
TREAT THE SKIES AS A FRIEND
AND THE PEOPLE AS THE SKIES

15:13.954 --> 15:15.164
[Bong-chan] Yes. I understand.

15:15.831 --> 15:17.416
Yes, sir. Yes.

15:18.626 --> 15:21.003
Yes, we will report back. Yes.

15:23.881 --> 15:24.965
Ah, goodness.

15:26.425 --> 15:28.969
Not a single person
alerted me this morning.

15:29.553 --> 15:30.429
[Jong-su] Sorry, sir.

15:30.512 --> 15:32.932
Until late this morning,
the atmosphere was stable

15:33.015 --> 15:35.434
and vertical temperature change
was expected to be very light.

15:36.018 --> 15:38.854
But surface temperatures rose
and stability became very poor.

15:38.938 --> 15:41.815
How did you analyze the AWS,
state and vertical wind field?

15:41.899 --> 15:44.151
- [Jong-su] There weren't any hail signals…
- Do you feel bad yet?

15:44.234 --> 15:45.653
…from the analysis results.

15:49.156 --> 15:50.741
[Bong-chan] But if we analyze the data

15:50.824 --> 15:53.577
from three hours ago,
or at least three perhaps…

15:54.620 --> 15:56.997
- [exhales]
- Hey. Aren't you off today?

15:57.665 --> 15:58.832
Your money, please.

15:59.333 --> 16:00.918
[Director Oh]
I'm in the middle of a meeting.

16:01.502 --> 16:04.546
I told you. I told you
it was hail on the report.

16:04.630 --> 16:08.509
With hail this bad, there must
have been an indicator signal somewhere.

16:09.218 --> 16:10.302
[Bong-chan] How frustrating.

16:11.053 --> 16:13.806
Let me see the adiabatic charts
in the affected area.

16:13.889 --> 16:15.766
Starting six hours ago.

16:15.849 --> 16:17.518
Mm-hmm.

16:17.601 --> 16:18.686
Um…

16:20.521 --> 16:21.897
Uh, okay, then. Twelve hours.

16:21.981 --> 16:23.273
COMPREHENSIVE CONTROL SYSTEM

16:24.650 --> 16:26.193
Now bring up three hours ago.

16:26.735 --> 16:29.321
- [beeps]
- Mm. Suwon.

16:29.989 --> 16:31.615
Not there. Incheon.

16:34.034 --> 16:35.869
[Bong-chan sighs]

16:36.745 --> 16:37.788
Icheon.

16:39.164 --> 16:40.374
Hey, wait a minute. That one.

16:40.457 --> 16:42.918
On the bottom. Zoom in a little.

16:43.002 --> 16:45.087
[keys clack]

16:47.798 --> 16:50.342
[serious music playing]

16:54.680 --> 16:55.806
[Bong-chan] Isn't that it?

16:57.057 --> 16:59.852
Uh-huh, signal's right there.

16:59.935 --> 17:01.145
- See?
- [sighs]

17:01.687 --> 17:04.148
[Bong-chan sighs]
My goodness.

17:06.025 --> 17:08.068
Yeah. You could see the clouds moving.

17:10.237 --> 17:12.281
Ah! Ah…

17:12.364 --> 17:13.657
Huh? Hmm?

17:14.992 --> 17:16.076
[sighs]

17:16.660 --> 17:18.746
You said it was real
as a ghost eating rice

17:18.829 --> 17:21.957
when I came over to show it to you.
Can you see it now? Obvious hail.

17:22.499 --> 17:24.126
All right. I'll buy you coffee.

17:24.209 --> 17:26.628
Huh? Just coffee?

17:27.880 --> 17:30.883
[sighs]
Director doesn't mean rich, you know.

17:30.966 --> 17:33.761
- Here, take it.
- Ah, no, no.

17:33.844 --> 17:35.012
Coffee's fine.

17:35.637 --> 17:37.806
- Thank you.
- Sure.

17:41.101 --> 17:43.812
- That's all. Well, then, bye. Go.
- O… okay.

17:43.896 --> 17:45.564
- Uh-huh. Yeah.
- Wait, um…

17:47.024 --> 17:48.942
Director Choi, had you seen this?

17:52.446 --> 17:54.198
[phone ringing]

17:55.616 --> 17:56.533
[Jong-su] I had.

17:57.701 --> 18:01.205
But I thought it was
just a temporary phenomenon.

18:01.288 --> 18:04.374
You can make your own judgment calls.

18:04.458 --> 18:07.086
But it should have at least
been mentioned in this report.

18:07.169 --> 18:09.546
- Sir, the numbers indicate--
- [Jong-su] I'm sorry, sir.

18:09.630 --> 18:12.341
It was my fault. I'll start a report now.

18:13.717 --> 18:14.802
[Bong-chan sighs]

18:14.885 --> 18:18.347
Call the Aviation Meteorologist
and say it was our mistake.

18:19.264 --> 18:21.809
Reach out to the Expressway Corporation
and the RDA,

18:21.892 --> 18:23.894
and find out about any crop damage.

18:23.977 --> 18:25.604
[employees] Yes, sir.

18:26.814 --> 18:28.190
A short phenomenon?

18:28.273 --> 18:31.777
You think saying nonsense will cover up
you missing all the signs?

18:35.280 --> 18:36.698
We don't just broadcast the weather.

18:36.782 --> 18:38.867
We're meant to forecast it,
for God's sake.

18:41.036 --> 18:42.579
I can't believe this.

18:45.499 --> 18:47.876
Sir, the reporters are waiting for us.

18:50.379 --> 18:52.005
[sighs]

18:52.089 --> 18:53.966
Wonderful. I love that they're punctual.

18:56.343 --> 18:58.178
Director Choi, go handle it.

18:58.971 --> 19:00.889
I have to meet
the Administration Director.

19:01.890 --> 19:03.058
[sighs]

19:08.272 --> 19:10.983
[gloomy music playing]

19:25.247 --> 19:26.999
[groans]

19:36.884 --> 19:39.428
Sir, you know
that I told you about the hail.

19:39.511 --> 19:41.763
Could you put that in your report for me?

19:42.306 --> 19:43.765
What for?

19:43.849 --> 19:46.476
You said so yourself. The best
of the best are there, am I right?

19:47.853 --> 19:50.230
I wanna go.

19:50.314 --> 19:51.690
- [chuckles]
- The best?

19:51.773 --> 19:53.692
Maybe years ago, man.

19:53.775 --> 19:54.943
What?

19:55.027 --> 19:59.323
It's changed a bit. I call it
Aoji Coal Mine that does weather.

19:59.406 --> 20:00.449
[chuckles]

20:04.203 --> 20:05.495
[Asst. Director Park]
I was told you need these

20:05.579 --> 20:07.497
for the ex-post analysis of the hail.

20:07.581 --> 20:11.126
Uh, it's all the similar cases
since the 1990s.

20:11.877 --> 20:15.881
Uh, you know, our team's been here
overnight every day this week.

20:15.964 --> 20:18.967
Can't the Policy Office cover it?
Can you help us out?

20:19.051 --> 20:22.429
We would love to help you,
but, uh, Mr. Ko specifically said

20:22.512 --> 20:24.973
that he wants the report
to be from your team, though.

20:25.057 --> 20:27.351
So we have to analyze all that
and write a report

20:27.434 --> 20:28.936
and monitor the weather?

20:29.519 --> 20:31.396
- It's…
- When do you need it by?

20:31.480 --> 20:33.232
[Asst. Director Park]
He wants it by this weekend.

20:33.315 --> 20:35.567
Thanks. Thanks a lot.

20:35.651 --> 20:37.277
Yeah. Run away, Park.

20:37.361 --> 20:39.529
Did you finish
the numerical model I asked for?

20:40.656 --> 20:43.242
- It'll be done soon.
- Finish it quickly.

20:46.286 --> 20:48.830
[mouse clicking]

20:50.332 --> 20:52.876
Maybe you should do
the briefing today, you know, huh?

20:52.960 --> 20:54.795
If you have a heart.

20:54.878 --> 20:57.381
I'd be overstepping authority
since the Chief Director's here.

20:58.340 --> 21:01.051
We've been the public's punching bag
forever, he's used to it.

21:03.303 --> 21:05.764
[groans in pain]

21:07.766 --> 21:09.768
- [body thuds]
- [gasps]

21:09.851 --> 21:11.937
- Director Choi!
- Director Choi!

21:12.020 --> 21:13.689
- Oh, my god! What's going on?
- Oh, no!

21:13.772 --> 21:16.066
- Director Choi!
- What is happening?

21:16.149 --> 21:17.276
- I don't know.
- [Soo-jin] Sir!

21:17.359 --> 21:19.444
- Somebody call an ambulance!
- What happened? Did anyone see?

21:19.528 --> 21:20.988
- Someone get help!
- Director Choi!

21:21.071 --> 21:24.074
[siren wailing]

21:31.039 --> 21:33.166
[engine revs]

21:35.919 --> 21:37.379
[sighs]

21:37.462 --> 21:39.047
He'll be okay, think so?

21:39.131 --> 21:41.341
- I'm sure he's gonna make it.
- One moment.

21:42.342 --> 21:45.304
The Spokesperson's Office
is losing it. They want a meeting.

21:46.096 --> 21:49.474
[Soo-jin] They have to understand our
director just got taken to the hospital.

21:49.558 --> 21:51.685
How many ambulances have we had this year?

21:51.768 --> 21:54.688
What do we do? Someone has
to cover him and do the briefing.

22:02.696 --> 22:03.864
I can do it.

22:07.284 --> 22:09.578
[gloomy music playing]

22:30.348 --> 22:31.558
[Ki-jun] How is Director Choi?

22:31.641 --> 22:33.518
Uh, they had to take him to the hospital.

22:33.602 --> 22:34.811
[Ha-kyung] So we haven't heard.

22:35.353 --> 22:37.230
Who was that?

22:37.314 --> 22:39.441
Oh, just a reporter.

22:39.524 --> 22:42.486
She was asking me to change
the order of the questions.

22:42.569 --> 22:44.654
Hmm. What should I say?

22:44.738 --> 22:47.616
Hmm. They already did the basic briefing
about the hail today,

22:47.699 --> 22:50.327
- so you'll just fill in the details.
- Okay.

22:50.410 --> 22:51.369
Good luck.

22:54.498 --> 22:57.417
[serious music playing]

23:01.421 --> 23:03.548
[papers rustling]

23:06.593 --> 23:08.762
We will take some questions now.

23:08.845 --> 23:12.432
[breathes deeply]

23:15.727 --> 23:20.273
RESTRICTED AREA

23:20.357 --> 23:22.234
[phone vibrates]

23:23.360 --> 23:25.237
I'm at the hospital. Yeah.

23:25.946 --> 23:28.573
No, it sounds like
he's gonna be all right.

23:28.657 --> 23:29.658
Oh, one second.

23:29.741 --> 23:31.576
- Director Choi?
- [nurse] Taking him to his room.

23:31.660 --> 23:33.495
- [Bong-chan] His room?
- [nurse] Yes.

23:34.204 --> 23:36.414
Oh, Mrs. Choi. Are you okay?

23:36.957 --> 23:38.917
You didn't have to come.
You're always busy.

23:39.000 --> 23:40.127
Of course, I had to.

23:40.210 --> 23:42.587
- I'm so relieved it's not that bad.
- "Relieved"?

23:44.381 --> 23:45.298
Oh…

23:46.258 --> 23:50.428
He's been asking for a formal transfer
to the country for years now.

23:50.512 --> 23:51.763
Yeah.

23:51.847 --> 23:53.390
The doctor warned him a while ago

23:53.473 --> 23:55.600
that he had to be careful
and has high blood pressure.

23:56.184 --> 23:57.894
But you kept pushing, you kept pushing,

23:57.978 --> 24:00.355
saying, "Next year, we'll do it,"
every year.

24:00.939 --> 24:02.607
You're the reason why he landed here.

24:02.691 --> 24:04.359
Over what, a little hail?

24:04.442 --> 24:08.488
- It wasn't… There was more going on--
- I mean, you guys are always wrong.

24:08.572 --> 24:11.533
Why did you have to make it
a big deal this time?

24:11.616 --> 24:14.244
[sharp exhale]
Do you know what they all call you?

24:15.412 --> 24:17.497
- What?
- A human juicer.

24:17.581 --> 24:20.041
[Jong-su's wife] Because you squeeze
people till there's nothing left.

24:21.126 --> 24:24.796
I'm exhausted, just like
everyone that works for you.

24:25.630 --> 24:27.966
I'm really…
I'm really sorry, you know that.

24:28.049 --> 24:30.552
Yeah. Well, goodbye, sir.

24:30.635 --> 24:33.013
- Yes. It'll be okay. I'm sorry.
- Thank you for coming.

24:42.314 --> 24:43.440
Any news?

24:48.111 --> 24:51.072
Uh, Director Choi had a heart attack.

24:52.532 --> 24:54.451
He kept saying that his chest felt heavy.

24:54.534 --> 24:55.619
He did?

24:56.828 --> 24:58.246
Why didn't I know that?

24:59.539 --> 25:02.042
They said he's gonna be okay, right?

25:02.125 --> 25:04.920
They're gonna do some extensive testing,
then we'll know more.

25:05.003 --> 25:06.171
He'll be okay, though.

25:06.254 --> 25:08.006
[Bong-chan]
I don't want anyone calling him

25:08.089 --> 25:10.717
or going to visit him because we
don't want to stress him out, right?

25:10.800 --> 25:13.637
And while he's gone,
we'll put an interim on Team Two.

25:16.056 --> 25:17.557
Jin, you can do it.

25:17.641 --> 25:20.977
[trivial music playing]

25:21.061 --> 25:22.896
Sir, I'm getting married next month.

25:23.939 --> 25:26.316
You can manage till Mr. Choi returns, huh?

25:26.816 --> 25:27.943
For two weeks tops.

25:28.026 --> 25:29.778
So can you handle all that?

25:31.529 --> 25:33.907
She can barely handle what she does now.

25:33.990 --> 25:35.951
Huh? Whoa. Speak up.

25:36.034 --> 25:38.411
If you have a better idea, say it. What?

25:39.412 --> 25:40.997
- [Seok-ho] No, sir.
- [Bong-chan] Okay.

25:42.249 --> 25:45.460
That's the plan, then, okay? Great.

25:51.424 --> 25:52.842
Okay, then.

25:58.932 --> 26:00.934
[sighs]

26:16.574 --> 26:18.994
[phone vibrates]

26:23.164 --> 26:24.582
[Ki-jun] Hey, you on your way?

26:24.666 --> 26:27.711
No, I can't. I can't get away
for the reunion.

26:29.129 --> 26:30.880
Again? I can't go alone.

26:30.964 --> 26:34.301
I don't have a choice.
Director Choi is on a leave of absence.

26:34.384 --> 26:35.885
[sighs]

26:43.351 --> 26:44.811
I get it.

26:44.894 --> 26:47.856
I'll tell them you say hi.
Just focus on your work.

26:49.232 --> 26:52.193
It sounds like it's just for two weeks,
so we just have to make it till then.

26:53.028 --> 26:54.112
Okay.

26:59.993 --> 27:00.952
[sighs]

27:01.036 --> 27:04.289
[emotional music playing]

27:09.627 --> 27:16.634
INNOVATIVE WEATHER SERVICES
A STEPPING STONE TO PUBLIC SAFETY

27:18.219 --> 27:20.805
[bright music playing]

27:26.061 --> 27:27.771
[birds chirping]

27:48.166 --> 27:50.543
♪ I wanna know ♪

27:50.627 --> 27:52.962
♪ It must be something real ♪

27:53.046 --> 27:55.048
♪ I just can't stop thinkin' ♪

27:55.131 --> 27:56.883
♪ Thinkin' about you ♪

27:58.218 --> 28:00.053
♪ Want you to know ♪

28:00.136 --> 28:01.513
[Si-woo] Wow.

28:01.596 --> 28:02.847
It's incredible.

28:03.556 --> 28:05.016
[deep exhale]

28:08.353 --> 28:10.230
I wish Yu-jin can see this.

28:12.732 --> 28:14.609
♪ I just can't stop thinkin' ♪

28:14.692 --> 28:16.694
♪ Thinkin' about you ♪

28:27.122 --> 28:28.373
GLOBAL WARMING
AND THE IMPACT OF CLIMATE CHANGE

28:28.456 --> 28:31.668
[senior reporter] So basically,
it's gonna be hot this summer.

28:31.751 --> 28:32.836
It needs to be simpler.

28:32.919 --> 28:35.338
Like, "Worst summer ever."

28:35.422 --> 28:36.881
"Get ready to sweat."

28:36.965 --> 28:38.508
"Heat like a steam bath."

28:38.591 --> 28:41.344
Keep it to five syllables.
Your titles are too long.

28:41.428 --> 28:44.180
It's not that this summer's
gonna be especially hot.

28:44.264 --> 28:47.475
The average temperatures are rising.
One to two degrees from global warming.

28:47.559 --> 28:51.521
Oh, you really think people
give a crap about global warming?

28:51.604 --> 28:52.772
It just needs to be provocative.

28:52.856 --> 28:55.150
You need to think about
what average people read.

28:55.233 --> 28:57.694
- But then--
- Are you going to make me say it again?

28:57.777 --> 29:01.573
Okay. The goal is to make
air-conditioning sales go up.

29:01.656 --> 29:04.033
You know what company
has our biggest ad account?

29:04.117 --> 29:05.285
So we're an ad agency?

29:05.368 --> 29:07.078
Why don't we just report the weather?

29:07.162 --> 29:09.080
'Cause ads pay for you, they pay for me.

29:09.164 --> 29:10.707
How can we afford to be here?

29:10.790 --> 29:13.126
[senior reporter] Keep that in mind, huh?

29:13.209 --> 29:15.295
And maybe we could get a bonus for once.

29:16.296 --> 29:17.464
Okay?

29:18.339 --> 29:19.632
Go on.

29:19.716 --> 29:21.593
You can do it, all right?

29:21.676 --> 29:22.677
Provocative.

29:23.636 --> 29:25.263
[annoyed exhale]

29:28.892 --> 29:30.477
[phone vibrates]

29:35.231 --> 29:38.526
LEE SI-WOO

29:38.610 --> 29:40.737
- What?
- [Si-woo] Look at these!

29:42.906 --> 29:44.324
I'M MAKING A SEAL TODAY
WHY?

29:44.407 --> 29:45.700
LOOK AT THESE VIEWS
THEY'RE NICE

29:48.953 --> 29:49.913
[phone vibrates]

29:49.996 --> 29:52.749
ISN'T IT AWESOME?

29:52.832 --> 29:54.876
Wow! I hit the jackpot today!

29:59.881 --> 30:01.341
That is a fairy cloud.

30:02.091 --> 30:05.303
I've only seen it once before.
I'm so lucky.

30:05.386 --> 30:06.763
Ugh.

30:09.349 --> 30:10.600
She saw them?

30:14.062 --> 30:16.064
[birds chirping]

30:20.819 --> 30:23.571
[light music playing]

30:29.828 --> 30:32.580
[grunting]

30:35.750 --> 30:37.460
Hey, Chief!

30:41.548 --> 30:44.801
Not this guy again.
[sighs]

30:44.884 --> 30:46.219
You win.

30:47.095 --> 30:48.096
I give up.

30:49.514 --> 30:51.641
[machine humming]

30:53.810 --> 30:57.230
So the antenna's operational
and nothing's wrong with it.

30:57.313 --> 30:59.357
But I could have told you that
on the phone.

30:59.440 --> 31:02.026
I had to see it
with my own eyes to trust it.

31:02.110 --> 31:04.821
And I really wanted to see you
in case you got lonely.

31:07.031 --> 31:09.242
So you think
that everything's operating well?

31:09.325 --> 31:10.743
- Yes.
- [door closes]

31:10.827 --> 31:13.371
You know the way out. I have work to do.

31:13.454 --> 31:15.707
It's just that we're only in March,

31:15.790 --> 31:19.419
and the temperatures are strangely low,
especially looking at inland averages.

31:19.502 --> 31:22.380
You have to go to the Gangwon Office.
They'll know.

31:26.342 --> 31:27.343
Oh.

31:27.427 --> 31:29.137
GANGWON REGIONAL OFFICE
OF METEOROLOGY

31:29.220 --> 31:31.055
[phone rings]

31:31.139 --> 31:32.223
Hello. How can I help you?

31:32.807 --> 31:35.852
Yes, hello. I saw surface temperatures
in Gangwon are off.

31:35.935 --> 31:37.061
Could you check them, please?

31:37.145 --> 31:38.605
Oh, yeah, sure.

31:39.606 --> 31:41.316
[Si-woo] Yeah, and I also wanna know

31:41.399 --> 31:44.777
Pyeongchang, Chuncheon,
Hongcheon, Hoengseong, and Wonju.

31:44.861 --> 31:46.779
If you can.
If it's not too much trouble for you.

31:46.863 --> 31:49.741
Just a minute. Pyeongchang.

31:51.618 --> 31:52.702
Chuncheon.

31:53.620 --> 31:54.495
Hongcheon.

31:54.579 --> 31:55.830
And where else?

31:55.914 --> 31:57.248
Hoengseong and Wonju.

31:57.332 --> 31:59.876
- Okay. Hoengseong and Wonju.
- [mouse clicks]

31:59.959 --> 32:02.295
- One moment.
- So sorry, but can you please hurry?

32:02.378 --> 32:04.672
- It's urgent.
- Wonju. Oh, no.

32:05.965 --> 32:07.634
Hello. This is Um.

32:08.217 --> 32:09.260
What is it?

32:09.344 --> 32:12.847
Yes, uh, I need Pyeongchang, Chuncheon,

32:12.931 --> 32:16.976
Hongcheon, Hoengseong,
and Wonju surface temperatures, please.

32:17.977 --> 32:19.270
GANGWON PROVINCE

32:19.354 --> 32:22.315
Oh, you're seeing wind coming in.

32:22.398 --> 32:24.233
It's a reaction to the sun's radiation.

32:24.317 --> 32:26.110
It happens from time to time.

32:26.194 --> 32:27.278
It'll level itself out.

32:27.362 --> 32:29.447
I don't think that's what's going on here.

32:29.530 --> 32:30.823
Huh?

32:32.450 --> 32:34.827
- Well, thanks for your help.
- [phone clacks]

32:35.662 --> 32:37.872
What do you mean by-- Are you there?

32:39.624 --> 32:41.751
What a rude little… Who was that?

32:41.834 --> 32:43.836
I, uh… I forgot to get his name.

32:45.129 --> 32:46.631
You forgot? That's important.

32:46.714 --> 32:49.842
If you knew his name, there's no way
some intern would talk to you that way.

32:50.593 --> 32:51.552
Sorry, sir.

32:51.636 --> 32:53.554
- [phone clacks]
- Jeez.

32:53.638 --> 32:54.973
[tongue clicks]

32:58.351 --> 33:00.269
- By the way, sir.
- Hmm?

33:00.353 --> 33:02.689
Did you hear the rumor coming from HQ?

33:02.772 --> 33:04.524
No. What happened?

33:04.607 --> 33:06.859
I heard that the director
for Team Two is out.

33:06.943 --> 33:08.277
They need a replacement.

33:09.988 --> 33:11.114
So what?

33:11.197 --> 33:13.616
You know, you have to go back someday.

33:14.409 --> 33:15.493
No, thanks.

33:16.077 --> 33:18.037
It was a pain in the ass.

33:18.121 --> 33:19.622
Even if they begged.

33:19.706 --> 33:22.834
Well, if you stay away from home too long,

33:22.917 --> 33:24.585
I heard your family
can forget who you are.

33:26.212 --> 33:27.964
Like you didn't exist.

33:28.047 --> 33:29.340
[sighs]

33:36.514 --> 33:39.434
[touching music playing]

33:46.482 --> 33:49.610
BO-MI'S DAD

33:49.694 --> 33:51.696
[line ringing]

33:58.411 --> 34:00.121
- Please. Oh.
- [Hyang-rae] Hello?

34:00.621 --> 34:02.290
I didn't know if you were gonna answer me.

34:02.373 --> 34:04.000
What? You don't
always pick up when I call?

34:05.084 --> 34:06.377
Oh, well…
[sighs]

34:07.378 --> 34:08.421
Are things good?

34:09.005 --> 34:11.215
Well, could you do anything
if they weren't?

34:11.299 --> 34:13.134
Hey, don't do that.

34:13.217 --> 34:16.054
Be nice to your husband.
I haven't seen you in about--

34:16.137 --> 34:17.597
[Hyang-rae] Why did you call?

34:18.473 --> 34:19.474
Bo-mi there?

34:20.600 --> 34:22.769
Bo-mi, it's Dad.

34:22.852 --> 34:23.895
[Bo-mi] No.

34:24.604 --> 34:27.190
- She can't.
- Oh, okay.

34:29.525 --> 34:30.526
'Kay. See you.

34:31.652 --> 34:33.488
[footsteps approaching]

34:33.571 --> 34:36.074
- [staff] Sir!
- Mm?

34:36.157 --> 34:37.992
Something you should see.

34:38.076 --> 34:43.748
NATIONAL METEOROLOGICAL CENTER
COMPREHENSIVE CONTROL SYSTEM

34:43.831 --> 34:46.626
[mysterious music playing]

34:52.965 --> 34:55.593
[phone vibrates]

34:55.676 --> 34:57.804
- Not now. I'm busy.
- [Tae-kyung] I'll be fast.

34:58.513 --> 35:00.556
Didn't you guys book Lian Wedding Hall?

35:00.640 --> 35:02.850
- Yeah, and why?
- Well, I called

35:02.934 --> 35:05.103
because Mom wanted me
to ask them something,

35:05.186 --> 35:07.522
and they never got your deposit.

35:07.605 --> 35:08.564
What?

35:08.648 --> 35:10.483
[Tae-kyung] Ki-jun
won't even pick up the phone.

35:10.566 --> 35:12.110
Is everything okay with you?

35:12.193 --> 35:14.987
Ki-jun's so thorough.
It has to be a problem with the venue.

35:15.071 --> 35:17.448
- It's time, everyone.
- I'll look into it, okay? I gotta go.

35:20.493 --> 35:24.497
[sighs]
All right. What's, uh…

35:24.580 --> 35:26.165
[Bong-chan] What's that little dangler?

35:26.249 --> 35:29.210
Convective clouds formed
from an unstable atmosphere.

35:29.293 --> 35:31.003
And what's the humidity over there?

35:31.504 --> 35:33.923
It's, uh, around 82 percent, I believe.

35:34.423 --> 35:35.925
What's the chance it turns to rain?

35:36.008 --> 35:37.927
Well, below 30 percent, Director.

35:38.010 --> 35:40.638
Okay. That's below the threshold
to issue an alert.

35:41.222 --> 35:42.682
Okay. Let's do our meeting.

35:45.518 --> 35:47.478
We will now discuss March 14's report.

35:47.562 --> 35:49.647
Let's hear
from the Satellite Center first.

35:49.730 --> 35:53.276
Yes. Hello, Headquarters. If you look
at the current movement of the clouds,

35:53.359 --> 35:55.611
you could see that a band
is developing to the northeast.

35:55.695 --> 35:58.156
Gangwon Office, your opinion
on this, please.

35:58.781 --> 36:01.033
Well, judging
from the characteristics of the area,

36:01.117 --> 36:02.785
it is unlikely that it'll lead to rain.

36:03.536 --> 36:04.871
[Si-woo] It's going to rain.

36:04.954 --> 36:06.289
I guarantee it!

36:06.372 --> 36:08.916
[Director Oh] Damn.
So you're really going nuts again?

36:09.000 --> 36:11.127
Hey, can't you see the sky out there?

36:11.878 --> 36:13.296
I sent you all the data.

36:14.297 --> 36:16.340
A storm's brewing here.

36:16.424 --> 36:18.176
- Soon, it's gonna get worse.
- I see the smudge.

36:18.259 --> 36:20.845
Now go sit down.
We're talking about it on our call.

36:20.928 --> 36:23.639
- Just wait over there till we're done.
- We don't have time.

36:23.723 --> 36:26.184
We have to put out a heavy rain advisory
in the whole metro area right now.

36:26.267 --> 36:27.560
I said calm down.

36:27.643 --> 36:30.605
Look, right here, right here.
See how high the surface temperatures are?

36:30.688 --> 36:32.607
The Gangwon Office said
that it's temporary.

36:32.690 --> 36:33.983
But the instability is too strong,

36:34.066 --> 36:36.861
and there's a high chance that it turns
into a serious rainstorm.

36:36.944 --> 36:39.280
- [Bong-chan] At this time, the…
- [sighs]

36:39.363 --> 36:41.282
Look. Look here.

36:41.991 --> 36:43.326
But this…
[sighs]

36:46.162 --> 36:48.456
[serious music playing]

36:48.539 --> 36:49.749
Metro Office, something to share?

36:49.832 --> 36:53.586
SEOUL METROPOLITAN OFFICE
OF METEOROLOGY

36:54.170 --> 36:58.216
The clouds that are forming
in the Gangwon area look unusual.

36:58.299 --> 37:00.468
Are you saying
that's a potential storm there?

37:00.551 --> 37:02.595
- [Director Oh] Yes, in an hour.
- And your source?

37:04.764 --> 37:06.891
- [sighs]
- Uh, just a moment.

37:09.435 --> 37:11.437
[Si-woo] An hour ago,
they were light clouds.

37:11.520 --> 37:14.941
However, passing the Chuncheon area,
they're rapidly approaching storm levels.

37:15.024 --> 37:16.651
I'll show you all the data right here.

37:17.818 --> 37:20.154
[serious music playing]

37:28.913 --> 37:30.414
[Seok-ho] There he goes again.

37:32.541 --> 37:34.919
He's the one who predicted the hail.

37:35.628 --> 37:38.214
- And so?
- Consider that.

37:44.303 --> 37:47.014
Do you know how dry
the atmosphere is right now?

37:47.098 --> 37:49.642
Even if the rain clouds are large enough
to be caught as an echo,

37:49.725 --> 37:53.562
all of it will be evaporated
long before it arrives in the city.

37:53.646 --> 37:55.481
[Si-woo] What if moisture
is added continuously

37:55.564 --> 37:57.525
as the formation continues
moving to the north?

38:00.611 --> 38:03.030
The temperature of the lower atmosphere
in this area is rising,

38:03.114 --> 38:05.491
so water vapor
is constantly being supplied.

38:05.574 --> 38:09.954
If you look at this, the clouds
were only two kilometers long an hour ago.

38:10.037 --> 38:13.040
But now, it's thicker.
Almost five or six kilometers.

38:13.124 --> 38:14.959
Furthermore, because
the surface temperature

38:15.042 --> 38:18.045
east of the metropolitan area is high
and the atmosphere is unstable,

38:18.129 --> 38:20.131
the clouds are more likely
to develop further

38:20.214 --> 38:22.258
as they move to this area
instead of evaporating.

38:22.341 --> 38:25.845
If all these numbers are correct,
then we have two to three hours

38:25.928 --> 38:28.597
before the entire metro area's storming.

38:33.728 --> 38:36.314
Then, according to you,
what's our chance of rain?

38:36.397 --> 38:38.274
Yes, so, uh…

38:38.357 --> 38:40.067
It should be about 18.7 or .8.

38:40.151 --> 38:42.903
- [Si-woo] Yes, that's right.
- [Dong-han] So you're saying…

38:42.987 --> 38:45.614
there's still well over
an 80 percent chance

38:45.698 --> 38:46.741
of clear skies today.

38:46.824 --> 38:50.411
The decimal, I would suggest,
isn't really necessary.

38:51.329 --> 38:55.082
Ah, well, then,
what's our course of action?

39:02.006 --> 39:05.509
[pensive music playing]

39:10.014 --> 39:12.266
[thunder rumbles]

39:27.615 --> 39:29.825
[wind blows]

39:31.035 --> 39:33.579
- [chimes]
- [birds chirping]

39:33.662 --> 39:36.123
[trilling]

39:44.715 --> 39:47.009
[phone vibrates]

39:48.636 --> 39:49.970
[Tae-kyung] I checked again

39:50.054 --> 39:52.473
and they're certain
that the deposit wasn't paid.

39:53.307 --> 39:55.893
They said that they told the groom
that the booking will be canceled

39:55.976 --> 39:58.104
if you don't pay the deposit
by end of the day.

40:03.776 --> 40:05.694
[Dong-han] It's not even summertime.

40:05.778 --> 40:07.154
It's the middle of March.

40:07.238 --> 40:10.491
A storm alert of over 20 percent odds
is a pointless alarm.

40:10.574 --> 40:12.493
Even by your numbers, it's no concern.

40:13.411 --> 40:15.913
You keep talking about a seasonal formula.

40:15.996 --> 40:18.249
Don't you think the data's
more important than the month?

40:18.332 --> 40:20.251
[phone vibrates]

40:20.334 --> 40:22.461
Forecasting is about probability.

40:22.545 --> 40:24.588
- And that's why we're always wrong.
- What's that?

40:24.672 --> 40:26.048
From the 17th typhoon last summer

40:26.132 --> 40:29.009
to the fog of the beginning of this year,
and most recently, the hail.

40:29.093 --> 40:31.846
Look what happened because you
were too obsessed with probabilities.

40:31.929 --> 40:33.097
Why do we even have forecasters, then?

40:33.180 --> 40:35.766
Why not just read the averages
of the computers and post them?

40:35.850 --> 40:38.185
[phone vibrates]

40:39.395 --> 40:40.938
POWER OFF

40:42.314 --> 40:44.608
Weather is about flow.

40:44.692 --> 40:45.693
You can't throw that out

40:45.776 --> 40:47.403
'cause of a funny-looking signal,
you know.

40:48.279 --> 40:50.281
Sudden shifts
can always disrupt that flow.

40:50.364 --> 40:52.950
Even small changes
can ripple into huge sudden storms.

40:53.033 --> 40:54.410
Are you teaching us now?

40:55.244 --> 40:56.370
No.

40:56.454 --> 40:58.998
I'm just saying there's
a bigger problem here to address.

40:59.081 --> 41:01.584
[Director Oh] Come on. That's it. Move.

41:02.501 --> 41:03.711
All right.

41:04.378 --> 41:06.005
Ha-kyung, substitute director.

41:06.755 --> 41:08.841
You should make a decision now.
[exhales]

41:08.924 --> 41:10.968
[pensive music playing]

41:16.557 --> 41:17.933
Let's do it like this.

41:20.978 --> 41:22.813
[serious exhale]

41:24.482 --> 41:27.276
Metro Office has suggested
a reasonable hypothesis.

41:27.359 --> 41:29.695
However, 18's too low for a storm alert.

41:30.446 --> 41:33.616
There's not enough evidence
or precedent available.

41:33.699 --> 41:36.327
- I told you I would show you the data--
- That's it.

41:36.410 --> 41:38.329
Our office will make a final assessment

41:38.412 --> 41:40.581
on the metro alert
after watching for a little.

41:41.540 --> 41:45.211
During that time, the Metro Office
can provide us with their source data.

41:46.504 --> 41:48.464
[Ha-kyung] Let's move on
to the weekend weather.

41:53.969 --> 41:56.013
[serious music playing]

41:56.722 --> 41:58.098
Hey!

41:59.475 --> 42:00.684
[breathes angrily]

42:04.355 --> 42:07.024
[Seok-ho] He's not gonna let it go.

42:08.734 --> 42:10.819
- [Myung-ju] You know him?
- Lee Si-woo.

42:11.445 --> 42:14.156
I worked with him
on Baengnyeong Island when I started.

42:14.240 --> 42:16.992
- Hmm.
- He's usually a pretty mellow guy.

42:17.076 --> 42:20.788
But then, he has some unorthodox theory
and he won't shut up.

42:20.871 --> 42:22.498
- [scoffs]
- [sucks teeth]

42:22.581 --> 42:23.874
But what bothers me is

42:24.458 --> 42:27.169
when he digs his heels in this hard,
sometimes he's right.

42:27.253 --> 42:29.713
[phone vibrates]

42:31.840 --> 42:33.425
[chuckles]

42:35.594 --> 42:37.721
[Si-woo] Seok-ho, hey, it's me.

42:37.805 --> 42:39.139
[sighs]
What do you want?

42:39.223 --> 42:41.100
[Si-woo] It's your job
to announce alerts, right?

42:42.351 --> 42:43.769
Yeah, it is. So what do you want?

42:44.728 --> 42:45.938
I just know a storm's here.

42:46.730 --> 42:48.232
Jeez, hey.

42:49.149 --> 42:50.442
[sighs]

42:51.193 --> 42:52.945
I can't do it.

42:53.028 --> 42:56.031
You're really gonna let your office
ignore this like you did the hail?

42:56.115 --> 42:57.241
Hey, uh--

43:00.953 --> 43:02.913
[sighs]
I swear he's crazy.

43:04.957 --> 43:07.459
All right, then.
Uh, no other action items, right?

43:07.543 --> 43:08.502
[woman] No, sir.

43:08.586 --> 43:09.795
[Bong-chan] Mm-hmm. Okay.

43:09.878 --> 43:11.797
[Ha-kyung] We'll adjourn the meeting here.

43:11.880 --> 43:13.674
- Thank you, sir.
- [Ha-kyung] Thanks, everyone.

43:13.757 --> 43:15.259
- Thank you.
- [Bong-chan] Yes, thank you.

43:15.342 --> 43:16.927
[woman] Bye. See you tomorrow.

43:19.305 --> 43:21.974
[yells]
Are you insane? What's your problem?

43:23.434 --> 43:25.352
[indistinct murmurs]

43:27.521 --> 43:28.439
[Bong-chan] What is it?

43:29.023 --> 43:32.151
The Metropolitan Office just put out
a storm advisory.

43:32.776 --> 43:33.777
[Bong-chan] What?

43:37.615 --> 43:38.574
You did this?

43:39.992 --> 43:43.579
Who would publish this without reporting
to the director first, huh?

43:43.662 --> 43:45.956
She won't accept my reports.
That's the reason why.

43:46.540 --> 43:48.208
[Seok-ho] Starting from the hail signal,

43:48.917 --> 43:50.586
she ignored me
and she said it was too low.

43:52.087 --> 43:53.505
What's he saying?

43:54.840 --> 43:58.093
There was a report from the Seoul
Metropolitan Office about a hail signal.

43:58.177 --> 44:01.513
The first one who detected it
was that guy you just spoke to.

44:02.681 --> 44:04.350
The probability was below five percent.

44:04.433 --> 44:06.101
It was five, if you rounded it out.

44:08.354 --> 44:11.231
Okay, so you declared
a strong weather alert

44:11.315 --> 44:14.318
without permission
from your director? Hmm?

44:14.401 --> 44:17.613
If you're gonna go rogue,
why do we pay for your superior?

44:17.696 --> 44:18.864
There's a hierarchy here.

44:18.947 --> 44:21.367
If you want to do things your way,
start your own company.

44:22.868 --> 44:24.244
I'm sorry, sir.

44:27.456 --> 44:29.333
[serious music playing]

44:29.416 --> 44:32.628
[Bong-chan] An advisory has been issued.
So keep your posts.

44:33.921 --> 44:35.798
I need to talk with you.

44:35.881 --> 44:37.424
Yes, sir.

44:45.641 --> 44:47.226
[sighs]

44:48.644 --> 44:50.062
My god.

44:52.314 --> 44:54.274
[sighs]

44:57.152 --> 44:59.655
What do you mean
you didn't report to Director Choi?

45:01.031 --> 45:03.659
Like you heard, sir,
the probability was too low.

45:06.120 --> 45:07.329
What I meant…

45:08.163 --> 45:10.791
is why did you make that decision,
skipping the director?

45:10.874 --> 45:12.042
[Bong-chan] Why?

45:17.965 --> 45:19.049
[sighs]
Okay.

45:19.716 --> 45:21.301
Write a report on it.

45:23.303 --> 45:25.013
Shut your mouth.

45:25.097 --> 45:27.808
If it doesn't rain in an hour,
we're both completely dead.

45:27.891 --> 45:30.102
[Si-woo] Don't worry. It's going to.

45:31.395 --> 45:32.312
Was it you?

45:33.647 --> 45:36.608
Are you the one who issued an advisory
without permission from Headquarters?

45:38.944 --> 45:40.779
Yes. It was me.

45:42.072 --> 45:45.284
Do you know how much it costs to declare
a single case of severe weather?

45:45.868 --> 45:48.120
And if it's wrong,
will you take the blame for it?

45:50.706 --> 45:52.124
And did you, the interim director,

45:52.207 --> 45:55.377
take full responsibility
for the incorrect hail forecast?

45:55.461 --> 45:56.670
[Ha-kyung] What did you say?

45:56.753 --> 45:59.840
No, not incorrect. You didn't
report it to anyone at all, did you?

46:00.549 --> 46:02.384
[Si-woo] I heard about
the whole situation.

46:02.468 --> 46:05.512
But, you know, even though you're busy
with all the wedding planning,

46:05.596 --> 46:08.557
isn't it a bit awkward
that a whole report was missed?

46:08.640 --> 46:11.894
You're a forecaster. You hold
the public's trust and confidence.

46:11.977 --> 46:14.688
You shouldn't throw that all away
because of your home life.

46:16.356 --> 46:18.609
- And you are?
- Lee Si-woo is my name.

46:19.526 --> 46:20.402
Lee Si-woo.

46:20.486 --> 46:23.280
You ask me to take responsibility
for this forecast?

46:23.363 --> 46:25.741
[Si-woo] If I may share with you
my actual responsibilities,

46:25.824 --> 46:29.077
I predict and forecast weather
based on the data I have collected.

46:29.161 --> 46:31.205
I'm confident about my forecasts.

46:31.288 --> 46:34.625
Completely. And that confidence comes
from doing what I know is proper.

46:34.708 --> 46:36.627
That's true with the hail situation
as well.

46:36.710 --> 46:40.839
Oh, so you're saying you don't like
the way I've been doing my job here?

46:40.923 --> 46:42.925
Well, of course, you have
your wedding to think of,

46:43.008 --> 46:45.511
- so I do understand.
- Hey, you!

46:45.594 --> 46:47.221
It's Lee Si-woo, Metro Office.

46:49.473 --> 46:50.599
Hey, Lee Si-woo.

46:50.682 --> 46:52.518
[snickers]
Just don't leave there.

46:53.143 --> 46:54.978
Why? You coming here?

46:55.562 --> 46:56.855
Just don't.

46:56.939 --> 46:58.482
TRAFFIC MONITORING OFFICE

47:02.694 --> 47:04.446
Yes. Uh-huh.

47:05.405 --> 47:07.199
[keyboard clacking]

47:10.035 --> 47:11.828
HEAVY RAIN ADVISORY
IN METROPOLITAN AREA

47:11.912 --> 47:14.498
HEAVY RAIN ADVISORY
IN METROPOLITAN AREA

47:14.581 --> 47:15.874
[notification alert tone]

47:15.958 --> 47:18.710
HEAVY RAIN ADVISORY
IN METROPOLITAN AREA

47:18.794 --> 47:20.963
EMERGENCY DUTY NOTIFICATION
MARCH 14

47:22.589 --> 47:24.675
ALL EMPLOYEES,
PLEASE REPORT TO EMERGENCY DUTIES

47:24.758 --> 47:25.968
UNTIL THE SITUATION IS RESOLVED

47:28.303 --> 47:30.806
HEAVY RAIN ADVISORY
IN METROPOLITAN AREA

47:33.267 --> 47:35.602
[man] Heavy rain advisory
in all coastal areas.

47:36.270 --> 47:37.646
Patrol ships on duty.

47:37.729 --> 47:40.190
Provide nearby vessels of safety protocol.

47:40.274 --> 47:42.484
- Ship Two on the way.
- Loud and clear, understood.

47:44.444 --> 47:47.281
[alarm wailing]

47:52.953 --> 47:54.454
[man] Double check that.

47:57.457 --> 47:59.167
[squeaks]

48:00.627 --> 48:01.878
[gushing]

48:09.136 --> 48:11.179
They're inspecting our boats.
It's ridiculous.

48:11.263 --> 48:14.016
Okay. Inspect all you want.
We're not gonna go out. You're happy?

48:14.099 --> 48:15.601
[yells, grunts]
Jeez.

48:17.686 --> 48:20.022
- [man] Hey, over there.
- Get over here.

48:20.105 --> 48:22.232
[indistinct chatter]

48:22.316 --> 48:23.984
Good.

48:24.067 --> 48:26.320
[clanks]

48:30.324 --> 48:31.283
More water now?

48:31.366 --> 48:33.035
[engine rumbles]

48:40.792 --> 48:46.757
HEAVY RAIN ADVISORY ISSUED
FOR METROPOLITAN AREA

48:46.840 --> 48:49.176
HEAVY RAIN ADVISORY
IN METROPOLITAN AREA

48:51.553 --> 48:53.388
SEOUL METROPOLITAN OFFICE
OF METEOROLOGY

48:57.392 --> 48:59.770
[sighs]
What now?

49:01.480 --> 49:05.651
Oh, that woman from Headquarters,
she won't actually come here, will she?

49:05.734 --> 49:07.486
There's no way she would, yeah.

49:07.569 --> 49:08.528
[sighs]

49:09.279 --> 49:11.698
She was just angry at you
because you were being so…

49:11.782 --> 49:12.699
the way you always are.

49:13.700 --> 49:14.785
She's here.

49:17.996 --> 49:20.207
[heels clacking]

49:23.001 --> 49:26.129
[Director Oh] Uh, I'm gonna go smoke.
She's here to see you.

49:26.213 --> 49:27.839
- Bye.
- [Ha-kyung] Mr. Lee Si-woo?

49:30.217 --> 49:31.551
[door closes]

49:38.183 --> 49:40.686
- You're really here.
- Are we friends?

49:40.769 --> 49:41.978
No.

49:42.062 --> 49:44.439
And yet you blab on
about something personal.

49:45.524 --> 49:49.695
- Well, you keep on ignoring my forecasts.
- Or just using my own judgment.

49:49.778 --> 49:53.365
Well, you didn't report it to anyone.
And people suffered for it.

49:53.448 --> 49:55.575
Do you know about the cost placed
on the public's taxes

49:55.659 --> 49:57.452
to announce a severe weather warning?

49:57.536 --> 50:00.622
Billions of won spent
on a five percent chance of hail?

50:00.706 --> 50:02.332
I have to weigh the cost and probability.

50:02.916 --> 50:04.793
Still, you shouldn't ignore
a strong signal.

50:04.876 --> 50:07.921
When it rains in the morning,
and we told people the afternoon,

50:08.004 --> 50:09.673
the whole nation resents us for it.

50:09.756 --> 50:11.299
How would they react to a false alert?

50:12.259 --> 50:14.928
Ah, so you're really
just being conservative.

50:15.011 --> 50:16.263
What?

50:16.346 --> 50:19.015
You'll be blamed either way,
whether you get it right or you don't.

50:19.099 --> 50:21.143
So you prefer to save the money
and the budget.

50:21.727 --> 50:25.021
Dodge one bullet while you're taking fire
from two separate directions.

50:25.105 --> 50:26.606
Isn't that what you're trying to say?

50:30.694 --> 50:32.279
Don't worry about it.

50:32.362 --> 50:34.823
I know it's coming, the rain.

50:39.453 --> 50:41.747
[gentle music playing]

50:41.830 --> 50:43.206
Like your name.

50:43.915 --> 50:47.002
Yeah, Si-woo. Rain that comes on time.

50:47.836 --> 50:49.004
Lee Si-woo.

50:56.762 --> 50:59.181
[plopping]

50:59.264 --> 51:01.057
[thunder rumbles]

51:06.521 --> 51:09.149
[rain pattering]

51:12.027 --> 51:13.195
[bell jingles]

51:13.278 --> 51:14.613
[psychic] It's going to rain.

51:18.366 --> 51:21.828
[merry music playing]

51:45.727 --> 51:48.230
NAMSAN

51:48.313 --> 51:49.439
Whoa!

51:51.858 --> 51:52.818
Hey, sir.

51:52.901 --> 51:55.195
DONGJAK BRIDGE

51:57.989 --> 51:59.491
Yeah, I can see it.

52:01.368 --> 52:02.494
Wow.

52:08.041 --> 52:09.709
[sighs]
Jeez.

52:16.424 --> 52:19.052
[bright music playing]

53:04.764 --> 53:06.725
[blows air]

53:36.588 --> 53:37.881
For you.

53:38.548 --> 53:39.841
[Si-woo] It's pouring.

54:05.408 --> 54:07.077
[phone vibrates]

54:10.246 --> 54:12.207
[rain pattering]

54:14.751 --> 54:16.002
THIS IS URGENT

54:16.086 --> 54:17.587
GET BACK TO ME.

54:17.671 --> 54:19.172
[Tae-kyung] Did you check with Ki-jun?

54:19.255 --> 54:22.258
[uneasy music playing]

54:22.342 --> 54:23.426
WE SENT YOU AN E-MAIL CONFIRMING

54:23.510 --> 54:24.719
THE FINAL DRAFT
BEFORE WE START PRINTING

54:24.803 --> 54:27.097
[printer] We sent out an email
with the final proof of the design

54:27.180 --> 54:28.306
before we start printing.

54:28.390 --> 54:30.976
But the groom didn't get back to us.
Please check in with him.

54:31.059 --> 54:32.602
[travel agent] Honeymoon package
has been canceled…

54:32.686 --> 54:34.604
[events man] We have successfully canceled
your order of 200 mini gifts…

54:34.688 --> 54:36.481
[sewer] We finished
the basting for your dress.

54:36.564 --> 54:38.149
[photographer] We got a cancellation text.
Please get back to us.

54:38.233 --> 54:40.110
[Lian Hall employee] Your booking
has been canceled due to delayed payment.

54:40.193 --> 54:41.736
Please confirm.

54:48.159 --> 54:50.954
KI-JUN

54:52.622 --> 54:55.083
[operator] The person you are trying
to reach is unavailable.

54:55.166 --> 54:56.584
You will be connected to voicemail.

54:56.668 --> 54:58.920
Please leave a message after the tone.

54:59.004 --> 55:00.880
[tone beeps]

55:19.649 --> 55:20.942
What'd she say?

55:21.026 --> 55:22.068
[Tae-kyung sighs]

55:25.572 --> 55:27.949
Ha-kyung hasn't responded.

55:30.201 --> 55:33.329
I think we lost the wedding hall
reservation now, Mom.

55:41.463 --> 55:42.672
[sighs]

55:44.632 --> 55:46.760
[thunder rumbles]

55:56.269 --> 55:58.271
- [elevator dings]
- [automated voice] Doors opening.

56:04.861 --> 56:06.237
[automated voice] Doors closing.

56:23.046 --> 56:25.507
[uneasy music playing]

56:28.718 --> 56:31.721
[whirs, beeps]

56:36.434 --> 56:37.894
[door opens]

56:47.612 --> 56:49.280
[squeaks]

56:55.328 --> 56:57.038
[door closes]

56:57.122 --> 56:58.665
[door lock beeps]

56:58.748 --> 57:00.375
[Ha-kyung] The signals were simple.

57:00.458 --> 57:04.003
- [Ki-jun] Hey, come closer.
- [woman giggles]

57:04.087 --> 57:06.131
- [woman] Oh!
- [Ki-jun] Feel better now?

57:07.298 --> 57:09.843
Sometimes, they were sounds.

57:10.385 --> 57:11.427
[woman moans]

57:11.511 --> 57:13.680
[woman] Wow!
[chuckles]

57:15.598 --> 57:17.517
[Ki-jun and woman giggling]

57:17.600 --> 57:20.311
Sometimes, they were colors.

57:22.021 --> 57:24.441
[heels clacking]

57:43.418 --> 57:45.378
[somber music playing]

57:47.881 --> 57:50.383
And sometimes, vibrations.

58:20.371 --> 58:23.374
[dramatic music playing]

58:25.502 --> 58:27.629
[gasps, cries]

58:32.717 --> 58:35.386
They kept signaling to me…

58:37.180 --> 58:41.184
that nothing was safe in this world.

58:52.654 --> 58:54.364
[humming merrily]

58:59.410 --> 59:01.579
Just in case.

59:01.663 --> 59:02.872
[grunts]

59:05.500 --> 59:09.003
[door lock beeping]

59:09.087 --> 59:09.921
[door opens]

59:10.505 --> 59:11.422
Oh, hello.

59:13.007 --> 59:15.468
- [door closes]
- [door beeps]

59:18.012 --> 59:19.430
[metal clanks]

59:20.223 --> 59:21.808
[sighs]

59:24.102 --> 59:25.436
So what is it?

59:26.062 --> 59:27.146
I got food for a trip.

59:28.773 --> 59:30.817
It'll stop raining early tomorrow morning.

59:31.401 --> 59:32.569
[Si-woo] So no problem there.

59:38.866 --> 59:40.118
Oh, this?

59:40.201 --> 59:41.452
Just being thorough.
[chuckles]

59:41.536 --> 59:42.870
We're not going camping.

59:42.954 --> 59:45.248
I got a nice cabin. Mm.

59:47.083 --> 59:48.459
[plates clank]

59:49.043 --> 59:50.128
[sighs]

59:51.546 --> 59:52.589
We're over.

59:54.799 --> 59:55.758
What?

59:57.218 --> 59:58.511
We're over.

01:00:04.142 --> 01:00:06.227
[somber music playing]

01:00:06.311 --> 01:00:07.562
Out of nowhere?

01:00:08.146 --> 01:00:09.355
Not nowhere.

01:00:10.815 --> 01:00:14.110
I've been wanting
to break up with you a long while.

01:00:46.392 --> 01:00:48.436
2 MONTHS LATER

01:00:48.519 --> 01:00:51.147
[Jong-su] Wow, that star is so bright.

01:00:51.981 --> 01:00:54.025
The sky cleared up nicely.

01:00:54.901 --> 01:00:56.861
[Ha-kyung] No, that's a satellite, sir.

01:00:56.944 --> 01:00:58.196
Hmm.

01:00:59.197 --> 01:01:01.491
Why do you have to be
such a stickler all the time?

01:01:01.574 --> 01:01:03.576
I know it's a satellite.

01:01:04.160 --> 01:01:05.286
Oh, okay.

01:01:05.370 --> 01:01:06.621
[chuckles]

01:01:07.413 --> 01:01:10.333
It's that trait
that makes me trust you always.

01:01:10.416 --> 01:01:12.585
Even more so than my own wife, I think.

01:01:15.880 --> 01:01:17.632
I wasn't a stickler when it mattered.

01:01:18.549 --> 01:01:19.676
What?

01:01:20.343 --> 01:01:21.761
You mean the day it hailed?

01:01:23.346 --> 01:01:24.972
Hmm.

01:01:26.182 --> 01:01:27.975
[keyboard clacking]

01:01:29.185 --> 01:01:31.437
Director Choi, I think
you should check this out.

01:01:31.521 --> 01:01:33.523
Hmm?
[groans]

01:01:36.818 --> 01:01:37.944
What?

01:01:39.112 --> 01:01:40.321
It's nothing.

01:01:43.574 --> 01:01:45.076
[sighs]

01:01:48.788 --> 01:01:51.916
We were on standby all week
because of the fog.

01:01:52.834 --> 01:01:56.546
I know. You didn't report it
because you didn't want me to worry.

01:01:59.340 --> 01:02:00.758
I still should have gone to you.

01:02:00.842 --> 01:02:03.511
Do you think things
would have been different if you had?

01:02:04.262 --> 01:02:05.304
They wouldn't.

01:02:05.805 --> 01:02:07.598
I wouldn't have done anything.

01:02:08.099 --> 01:02:10.810
The fog in the West Coast area
was no joke.

01:02:11.602 --> 01:02:15.314
And we prevented
any major car or truck collisions

01:02:15.398 --> 01:02:16.899
along the highway, right?

01:02:18.234 --> 01:02:20.027
Nobody acknowledges things like that.

01:02:20.111 --> 01:02:23.072
Hmm. Why do you care
what they acknowledge?

01:02:23.156 --> 01:02:25.533
No one got hurt. That's what matters.

01:02:26.909 --> 01:02:28.411
Come back to us soon, sir.

01:02:28.494 --> 01:02:31.706
Oh? You didn't hear? I just resigned.

01:02:32.707 --> 01:02:34.834
- How could you?
- [sharp exhale]

01:02:34.917 --> 01:02:38.588
I'm gonna live the rest of my life
doing everything I couldn't do before.

01:02:38.671 --> 01:02:39.797
Why? Why?

01:02:39.881 --> 01:02:41.424
[giggles]

01:02:41.507 --> 01:02:43.176
My wife is so happy.

01:02:48.765 --> 01:02:49.766
So thank you.

01:02:50.725 --> 01:02:52.351
I couldn't have made the decision

01:02:52.435 --> 01:02:55.772
to retire early,
if the office didn't have you.

01:02:55.855 --> 01:02:59.817
I feel very safe
that you're ready to take the reins.

01:03:02.862 --> 01:03:05.740
[tranquil music playing]

01:03:08.826 --> 01:03:12.205
I feel so close to drowning
all because I miss the signals.

01:03:18.503 --> 01:03:20.963
What you see in front of yourself
right now isn't everything.

01:03:21.047 --> 01:03:23.049
It's the same for life
as it is for weather.

01:03:23.132 --> 01:03:24.300
You have to wait and see.

01:03:24.383 --> 01:03:26.636
It's not always gonna be hailing for you.

01:03:27.595 --> 01:03:32.725
Sunny days, cloudy days,
rainy days, and snowy days…

01:03:34.769 --> 01:03:36.729
all come and go.

01:03:37.647 --> 01:03:39.315
[Jong-su chuckles]

01:03:54.455 --> 01:03:57.166
PERSONNEL CHANGES
JIN HA-KYUNG: DIRECTOR

01:03:57.250 --> 01:03:58.876
What happens now?

01:03:58.960 --> 01:04:00.795
Well, she's smart.

01:04:01.420 --> 01:04:04.590
You think computers are doing
other people's jobs for them

01:04:04.674 --> 01:04:06.467
because they aren't smart enough?

01:04:06.551 --> 01:04:10.429
Experience is the most important quality
in a director.

01:04:10.513 --> 01:04:13.891
She's gonna be so high-strung every day,
lecturing everyone.

01:04:14.559 --> 01:04:17.270
But how? How's it gonna work, though?

01:04:18.104 --> 01:04:19.230
What?

01:04:19.313 --> 01:04:22.316
I mean, Mr. Han's going to return
from the honeymoon, right?

01:04:23.192 --> 01:04:25.403
Will they be okay when working together?

01:04:25.486 --> 01:04:27.280
What are they gonna do,
even if they're not?

01:04:27.363 --> 01:04:29.365
They can't quit their jobs
'cause they're fighting.

01:04:29.448 --> 01:04:32.743
The people around them
are going to be the ones that suffer, huh?

01:04:32.827 --> 01:04:34.579
- We're all gonna be in some--
- [doors open]

01:04:35.496 --> 01:04:37.373
- Hello, ma'am.
- Hello, ma'am.

01:04:37.456 --> 01:04:39.292
- [Seok-ho] Hello, Director.
- [man] Hello, ma'am.

01:04:39.375 --> 01:04:41.002
[women] Hello, ma'am.

01:04:41.085 --> 01:04:43.880
SAFE COUNTRY, PEACEFUL PEOPLE

01:04:47.174 --> 01:04:49.260
[phone rings]

01:04:50.344 --> 01:04:51.470
You saw it, right?

01:04:52.096 --> 01:04:53.598
The promotion list?

01:04:53.681 --> 01:04:55.558
Yes, it was just posted.

01:04:58.144 --> 01:04:59.437
No.

01:05:00.187 --> 01:05:02.231
I'm talking about Mr. Han.

01:05:03.941 --> 01:05:05.318
[Bong-chan sighs]
You didn't see it.

01:05:06.611 --> 01:05:08.487
They canceled his transfer.

01:05:12.325 --> 01:05:14.327
He's good at dealing with the press.

01:05:14.410 --> 01:05:17.371
I guess the Administrator
thinks highly of him because of that.

01:05:17.455 --> 01:05:19.624
He wants to keep him by his side.

01:05:20.333 --> 01:05:22.752
[awkward chuckle]
Ah.

01:05:23.794 --> 01:05:25.129
[sucks teeth]
You okay?

01:05:26.672 --> 01:05:29.383
I'd love for Chief Team Two
to still have you in charge.

01:05:30.843 --> 01:05:33.971
But you'll still see him around.
Is that okay with you?

01:05:38.309 --> 01:05:39.936
[sighs]

01:05:41.228 --> 01:05:44.690
I mean, don't you wanna get on
the high-powered track?

01:05:45.399 --> 01:05:47.860
And work toward
a real leadership position, possibly.

01:05:50.363 --> 01:05:53.449
Well, you spent enough time
on a forecast desk.

01:05:54.367 --> 01:05:57.536
Are you saying that I should leave
the Forecast Bureau?

01:05:57.620 --> 01:06:00.831
There's an opportunity
for those commissioned to Grade 5

01:06:00.915 --> 01:06:02.416
to be sent to WMO.

01:06:04.669 --> 01:06:07.421
I mean, you have
more than enough experience.

01:06:07.505 --> 01:06:09.715
I can recommend you. Huh?

01:06:12.343 --> 01:06:14.303
You're talking
about Geneva, Switzerland, right?

01:06:14.387 --> 01:06:18.432
Yeah, Geneva. It's for a year,
but you can extend it too.

01:06:19.308 --> 01:06:23.562
[Ha-kyung] The breakup wasn't the end
when it came to office romance.

01:06:24.605 --> 01:06:26.148
[door lock beeps]

01:06:28.567 --> 01:06:30.069
[door closes]

01:06:47.795 --> 01:06:50.673
[somber music playing]

01:06:58.097 --> 01:06:59.056
[light switch clicks]

01:07:01.350 --> 01:07:02.727
[beeps]

01:07:03.644 --> 01:07:05.896
[mysterious music playing]

01:07:10.234 --> 01:07:12.528
[line dials, rings]

01:07:12.611 --> 01:07:15.281
Tae-kyung, did you take
the TV from the living room?

01:07:15.364 --> 01:07:16.741
It's not there?

01:07:17.908 --> 01:07:20.995
Mom, did you take the TV
from Ha-kyung's place?

01:07:21.495 --> 01:07:23.289
Why would I take something from there?

01:07:23.998 --> 01:07:26.542
I wouldn't wanna risk
invoking Ha-kyung's wrath.

01:07:27.460 --> 01:07:30.254
[Mrs. Bae] Why? Is the TV gone?

01:07:30.337 --> 01:07:32.256
Uh, no. See you.

01:07:40.639 --> 01:07:42.475
[taps]

01:07:46.437 --> 01:07:48.147
[beeps]

01:07:51.692 --> 01:07:53.402
[beeps]

01:07:54.612 --> 01:07:56.113
Oh, my…

01:07:56.197 --> 01:07:59.617
OFFICE OF SPOKESPERSON
HAN KI-JUN

01:08:01.243 --> 01:08:03.287
[line ringing]

01:08:06.582 --> 01:08:07.958
No.

01:08:08.042 --> 01:08:09.710
[phone vibrates]

01:08:09.794 --> 01:08:12.171
OFFICE OF SPOKESPERSON
HAN KI-JUN

01:08:14.465 --> 01:08:16.509
Hello? So what's up?

01:08:17.468 --> 01:08:18.511
Huh?

01:08:19.136 --> 01:08:22.848
Ah, I guess I hit your number by accident.
[awkward chuckle]

01:08:23.891 --> 01:08:26.727
I'm doing good. Same as always, yeah.

01:08:27.561 --> 01:08:28.562
Um…

01:08:29.939 --> 01:08:32.441
Would you have taken the TV?

01:08:32.525 --> 01:08:35.194
Mm, yeah, I took it.

01:08:36.153 --> 01:08:38.405
- And the cooker?
- Yeah.

01:08:38.489 --> 01:08:39.865
The toothbrush sterilizer, too?

01:08:39.949 --> 01:08:42.743
You said to get everything together
and leave.

01:08:43.244 --> 01:08:46.831
I thought you meant
that I should take what I need. No?

01:08:47.706 --> 01:08:50.668
How… That's really what you thought?

01:08:51.293 --> 01:08:53.170
I meant get your stuff and leave.

01:08:53.879 --> 01:08:54.839
[sighs]

01:08:55.339 --> 01:08:59.385
What's really mine and what's yours,
we split the cost of everything.

01:08:59.468 --> 01:09:00.511
I left the fridge, right?

01:09:00.594 --> 01:09:02.930
So doesn't that mean
it all roughly ends up equal?

01:09:06.684 --> 01:09:08.686
And when are we going
to deal with the apartment?

01:09:09.478 --> 01:09:13.482
So, Ha-kyung, I've been thinking.
How about, uh…

01:09:14.525 --> 01:09:17.319
I'll give half the money back to you,
and I'll take it all.

01:09:18.445 --> 01:09:19.530
All of what?

01:09:19.613 --> 01:09:21.615
We both put our names down on the title.

01:09:22.241 --> 01:09:24.326
And it'd be messy
to sell it together or whatever.

01:09:24.410 --> 01:09:26.954
- This way, it's better for you too.
- [scoffs]

01:09:27.037 --> 01:09:30.040
You said I could keep it all
to make up for everything, didn't you?

01:09:30.124 --> 01:09:32.459
Yeah, I did say that.

01:09:32.543 --> 01:09:33.419
And then?

01:09:33.502 --> 01:09:35.921
The value went up. It went up a lot more.

01:09:36.547 --> 01:09:37.423
And so?

01:09:40.050 --> 01:09:42.303
Let's split it. Halvsies.

01:09:42.386 --> 01:09:45.389
[trivial music playing]

01:09:45.472 --> 01:09:47.057
[Ha-kyung] As expected,

01:09:47.141 --> 01:09:52.438
a breakup wasn't enough
to get this bastard out of my life.

01:09:57.776 --> 01:10:00.613
["I'll Tell You Today's Weather"
by Gaemi, Lee Joon Wha playing]

01:10:25.137 --> 01:10:26.513
[Si-woo] Like the wind,

01:10:26.597 --> 01:10:29.808
an affair might not be visible at first,
but it will leave a mark.

01:10:29.892 --> 01:10:30.976
Now you're in. Go to work.

01:10:31.060 --> 01:10:33.812
I just got reassigned.
I'm on Severe Weather Forecast, Team Two.

01:10:33.896 --> 01:10:34.813
I've been transferred.

01:10:34.897 --> 01:10:37.608
[Seok-ho] I don't think Director Jin
will be here for very long.

01:10:37.691 --> 01:10:39.902
[yells]
Han Ki-jun!

01:10:39.985 --> 01:10:41.695
- You leave me no choice.
- Do you want to fight?

01:10:41.779 --> 01:10:43.030
[Si-woo] Director Jin.

01:10:43.113 --> 01:10:46.033
I wanted to check in
and see how you were doing.

01:10:46.116 --> 01:10:47.284
Cheers!

01:10:47.368 --> 01:10:49.495
[Ha-kyung] I'll never date
a co-worker ever again.

01:10:49.578 --> 01:10:52.498
[Si-woo] Really? Never is a strong word.
